
The following directories are the source for these knots:

/imager/project2/scharein/ThesisAux/work/min-sticks/5to8/min
/imager/project2/scharein/ThesisAux/work/min-sticks/9C/min
/imager/project2/scharein/ThesisAux/work/min-sticks/links/min
/imager/project2/scharein/ThesisAux/work/min-sticks/10D/min

All are in configurations that minimize the MD-energy.
The xyz-axes are aligned with the principal axes of the knot,
with the largest moment of inertia corresponding to the y-axis,
and the smallest moment of inertia corresponding to the z-axis.

The knots are scaled so that the distance of closest approach of
any two non-adjacent edges is equal to 0.5.

					rob scharein
					19 feb 1998

